# Rio parser factories, declared explicitly rather than left to the ones RDF4J's own JARs carry.
#
# RDF4J declares its Rio factories through JPMS `module-info`, and shading discards those
# declarations — so in a fat JAR `ServiceLoader` finds only whichever legacy service file survived
# the merge, and `Rio.getParserFormatForFileName(...)` fails with
# "UnsupportedRDFormatException: Did not recognise RDF format object Turtle" for everything else.
# `mergeServiceFiles()` cannot repair that on its own; the converters carry the same file for the
# same reason.
#
# Only formats whose module is a declared dependency belong here: a class named here and absent from
# the JAR makes ServiceLoader throw and takes the whole registry down with it.
org.eclipse.rdf4j.rio.turtle.TurtleParserFactory
org.eclipse.rdf4j.rio.trig.TriGParserFactory
org.eclipse.rdf4j.rio.ntriples.NTriplesParserFactory
